    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0160" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg150"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.019 EAC/6–2245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-22T18:00:00+02:00">June 22, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 22—3:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6315. Cornea 296. For Erhardt. US delegation EAC has studied intensively Gen
                    McNarney’s recommendations rearrangements for Vienna (urtel 4933, June 19<anchor
                        n="73" xml:id="d118-f1"/>) and consulted Generals Flory and Snavely in
                    detail. Preliminary consultation UK delegation showed Brit intention introduce
                    several subsidiary issues all requiring reference to Moscow. Prolonged
                    consultations UK and French delegations reduced principal new issue to provision
                    of 3 airdromes.</p>
                <pb facs="0161" n="151" xml:id="pg151"/>
                <p>Today Mosely made detailed review Austrian issues with Soviet delegation. Soviet
                    delegation referring to Moscow tonight proposal for 3 airdromes. EAC meeting
                        Saturday<anchor n="74" xml:id="d118-f2"/> morning on Austria.</p>
                <p>Sent to Dept as 6315; rptd AusPolAd as 5.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
